1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,100
What if you lived in space for ten years?

2
00:00:02,617 --> 00:00:03,124
Day one.

3
00:00:03,124 --> 00:00:06,361
About two liters of fluid rush up toward your head.

4
00:00:06,361 --> 00:00:08,963
Astronauts call it puffy face, bird legs.

5
00:00:09,450 --> 00:00:10,017
Month one.

6
00:00:10,017 --> 00:00:14,384
Your spine and hips lose one to one and a half percent of their bone density,

7
00:00:14,384 --> 00:00:15,064
every month.

8
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:17,500
Like and subscribe for more what-ifs.

9
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:19,527
Meanwhile, your spine stretches.

10
00:00:19,527 --> 00:00:21,685
You can grow up to three percent taller.

11
00:00:22,183 --> 00:00:26,642
And each day in orbit brings a month or two of ground-level radiation.

12
00:00:26,642 --> 00:00:29,572
Ten years would blow past NASA's career limit.

13
00:00:30,083 --> 00:00:34,416
One astronaut on China's space station is about to stay a whole year.

14
00:00:34,416 --> 00:00:36,048
Full story on the channel.
